{"author":{"id":"3f8bad4585cb0f07c6570d9e31f06264af3b0abf48efbc5a44f56df5e7a9cd45"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790243145,"nonce":"kFBFN9DavHr+ejBotb8ilQH78w0=","message":"Shared Future implementation exposes core-owned caribou.Future with ready()/await(), plugin ABI resolve/reject, cross-thread Rooted\u003cFuture\u003e, and scheduler wait-token wakeup. Haxe and Wren interop fixtures now pass with a plugin future resolved from a worker thread. Zyntax still needs an adapter between zyntax_embed::runtime::ZyntaxPromise and caribou.Future (including stackless request_park/Pending behavior). The Python frontend cannot yet exercise that path: its upstream an_unsupported_form_is_named regression confirms async def is rejected as unsupported. Once Python async lowering exists, it should reuse the same Zyntax-to-Caribou future adapter rather than define another cross-language promise ABI.","files":null}]}